<task id="006" project="email-communication-solution-r4">
  <metadata>
    <title>BFF send-path — `AttachmentDriveItemIds` non-breaking rename + `Internet-Message-Id` / `In-Reply-To` capture</title>
    <phase>Wave 0 — Shared foundation (schema · ADR · server send-changes · retire OOB-email)</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>5</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>001, 005</dependencies>
    <blocks>012, 022, 060</blocks>
    <tags>bff-api, communication</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies `.cs` in `Sprk.Bff.Api` — non-breaking DTO contract change + post-send Graph read + Dataverse stamp on the live send path. FULL per CLAUDE.md §8; Step 9.5 gates + publish-size + CVE + placement justification required.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W0-C</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <fr-refs>FR-06</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Two BFF send-path changes, both required by FR-06:

    1. **Non-breaking `AttachmentDriveItemIds` rename.** Add `public string[]? AttachmentDriveItemIds { get; init; }` as the canonical attachment field on `SendCommunicationRequest`; mark the existing `AttachmentDocumentIds` `[Obsolete("Use AttachmentDriveItemIds")]`; normalize the two into one internal list at the entry of `CommunicationService.SendAsync()` (canonical wins when both set; alias use logs a deprecation warning). **Mirror the R3 task 002 implementation EXACTLY** — read `projects/x-email-communication-solution-r3/tasks/002-bff-dto-add-attachmentdriveitemids.poml` and apply the same pattern (obsolete attribute + scoped `#pragma warning disable CS0618` around the normalization read + structured warnings). Values are Microsoft Graph `driveItem` IDs, NOT `sprk_document` GUIDs — XML docs must say so.

    2. **Thread-id capture.** After a successful send, capture the real RFC-2822 `Internet-Message-Id` from the Graph-sent message and stamp `sprk_internetmessageid` on the `sprk_communication` record. For `reply`/`forward` sends, stamp `sprk_inreplyto` with the parent message's `Internet-Message-Id`. Capture is best-effort and MUST NOT fail the send (NFR-06). These columns (task 001) feed the W1 thread-continuity rung (task 012).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF engineer authoritative on `Services/Communication/` — `CommunicationService.SendAsync()`, the Graph `SendMail`/OBO path, and the `sprk_communication` write. Familiar with ADR-010 (`CommunicationModule` DI), ADR-019 (ProblemDetails), ADR-028 (central credential), and `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`.
  </role>

  <goal>
    `SendCommunicationRequest` exposes canonical `AttachmentDriveItemIds` + obsolete `AttachmentDocumentIds`; `SendAsync()` normalizes both at entry (canonical wins + deprecation warning). Post-send, `sprk_internetmessageid` is stamped on the record; `reply`/`forward` also stamp `sprk_inreplyto`. Capture failures are non-fatal. Build clean; existing + new Communication tests pass; publish-size + CVE reported; placement justification stated.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Empirical finding #3: `SendCommunicationRequest.cs` currently exposes ONLY `AttachmentDocumentIds`, a misleading name (values are Graph `driveItem` IDs). Empirical finding #4: `CommunicationService.cs` does NOT capture `Internet-Message-Id`. R3 designed the attachment rename (task 002, never executed); R4 executes it here AND adds the thread-id capture in the same send-path task since both edit `SendAsync()`.

      The rename is non-breaking (FR-06 / NFR-05): both fields accepted; R4 does NOT delete the alias (a later release removes it after callers migrate). Task 022 (client) adopts `attachmentDriveItemIds`; task 060 migrates DocumentEmailWizard (which ships wrong IDs today). The thread-id capture feeds task 012's rung-1 thread-continuity matching.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Models/SendCommunicationRequest.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationService.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/CommunicationEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file>projects/x-email-communication-solution-r3/tasks/002-bff-dto-add-attachmentdriveitemids.poml</file>
      <file>projects/x-email-communication-solution-r3/tasks/003-bff-internet-message-id-capture.poml</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project (FR-06 / NFR-05)">Non-breaking: BOTH `AttachmentDriveItemIds` and `AttachmentDocumentIds` MUST be accepted. Do NOT delete the alias in R4. Existing callers compile + send unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Mapping rule: alias-only → copy to canonical + deprecation warning; both set → canonical wins + warning. Mirror R3 task 002 exactly (scoped `#pragma warning disable CS0618`).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project (NFR-06)">`Internet-Message-Id` / `In-Reply-To` capture is BEST-EFFORT — a capture/stamp failure MUST NOT fail the send. Wrap in try/catch, log, proceed.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Communication services register via `CommunicationModule` only — add no DI registration outside it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Use the injected central `TokenCredential` / `IGraphClientFactory` for the post-send Graph read — MUST NOT `new` a credential or `ConfidentialClientApplication`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">No new error path — normalize input at `SendAsync()` entry; validation failures stay ProblemDetails.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-045">Task 005's ADR codifies the canonical send contract — confirm this task aligns (canonical attachment field + thread-id stamping).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project (§10)">Load `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`; state Placement Justification in PR; report publish-size delta (baseline ~49.63 MB incl. PDBs, ≈0 expected); confirm no new HIGH CVE; run `/conflict-check` before PR.</constraint>
  </constraints>

