    <patterns>
      <pattern name="DTO field obsoletion (non-breaking)" location="projects/x-email-communication-solution-r3/tasks/002-bff-dto-add-attachmentdriveitemids.poml">
        Mark old field `[Obsolete("Use X")]`; keep accepting it; normalize at single entry point; scoped `#pragma warning disable CS0618` around the read; structured deprecation warning on use.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Best-effort post-send Graph read" location="projects/x-email-communication-solution-r3/tasks/003-bff-internet-message-id-capture.poml">
        After `SendMail`, fetch the sent message's `internetMessageId` via Graph (using the injected client); stamp Dataverse; try/catch so failure never blocks the send.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read the R3 task 002 + 003 POMLs in full — this task executes their combined intent. Load `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`.</step>
    <step order="2">Read `SendCommunicationRequest.cs` (confirm only `AttachmentDocumentIds` present) + `CommunicationService.SendAsync()` (locate entry point + post-send site + the `sprk_communication` write).</step>
    <step order="3">Edit `SendCommunicationRequest.cs`: add `AttachmentDriveItemIds` (init-only `string[]?`, XML doc "Microsoft Graph driveItem IDs — NOT `sprk_document` GUIDs; canonical per ADR-045"); mark `AttachmentDocumentIds` `[Obsolete("Use AttachmentDriveItemIds.")]` with updated XML doc.</step>
    <step order="4">Edit `SendAsync()` entry: add the normalization block (alias-only → copy + warning; both set → canonical + warning) inside a scoped `#pragma warning disable CS0618`; replace downstream reads of `AttachmentDocumentIds` with the canonical local.</step>
    <step order="5">Edit `SendAsync()` post-send: after a successful `SendMail`, fetch the sent message's `internetMessageId` via the injected Graph client; stamp `sprk_internetmessageid` on the record. If `mode` is `reply`/`forward`, resolve the parent's `Internet-Message-Id` and stamp `sprk_inreplyto`. Wrap the whole capture in try/catch — log + proceed on failure (NFR-06).</step>
    <step order="6">Add/update unit tests in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/`: (a) alias-only path logs deprecation + sends; (b) both-set path prefers canonical + warns; (c) post-send stamps `sprk_internetmessageid`; (d) capture failure does NOT throw from `SendAsync` (per NFR-08 test obligation).</step>
    <step order="7">`dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` (clean, no warnings outside the scoped pragma) + `dotnet test tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ --filter Communication` (green).</step>
    <step order="8">`dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o deploy/api-publish/`; report compressed size + delta vs ~49.63 MB. Expected ≈ 0.</step>
    <step order="9">`dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` — confirm no new HIGH CVE.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor gates: `/conflict-check` (BFF PR gate); `code-review` on the diff; `adr-check` against `spec.md` (ADR-010/019/028/045). Address Critical findings.</step>
    <step order="10">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: mark task 006 ✅; confirm dependents 012/022/060 unblocked.</step>
    <step order="11">Update `current-task.md` per task-execute: status → completed; record decisions (canonical-prefer-with-warning; best-effort capture).</step>
  </steps>

