  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`SendCommunicationRequest.AttachmentDriveItemIds` exists (init-only `string[]?`) with XML doc stating "Microsoft Graph driveItem IDs".</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`AttachmentDocumentIds` has `[Obsolete("Use AttachmentDriveItemIds...")]`; both fields are accepted (non-breaking).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`SendAsync()` normalizes both into one canonical list; alias-only + both-set paths each log the correct warning.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Post-send stamps `sprk_internetmessageid`; `reply`/`forward` also stamp `sprk_inreplyto`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A capture/stamp failure does NOT fail the send (test-verified; NFR-06).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Post-send Graph read uses the injected credential/client — no `new` credential (ADR-028).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Build clean (no warnings outside the scoped pragma); Communication tests pass; publish-size delta + CVE reported; `/conflict-check` run; Placement Justification in PR.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Executes the combined intent of R3 tasks 002 (attachment rename) + 003 (message-id capture) in one send-path task — both edit `SendAsync()`, so splitting them would double the diff surface on the same method. Read both R3 POMLs first.

    R4 does NOT delete `AttachmentDocumentIds` — the alias stays until callers migrate (later release). Task 060 fixes DocumentEmailWizard (line 494) which currently ships `sprk_document` GUIDs; the deprecation warning fires from there until then.

    `sprk_internetmessageid` + `sprk_inreplyto` are text columns from task 001 (both String 255 indexed). Confirm they exist before stamping (task 001 dependency).
  </notes>

